  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow-sm">Why it matters</div>
    <h2>Protecting the water supply, not just the building.</h2>
    <p>Backflow prevention assemblies protect Portland's drinking water supply from contamination. If water pressure drops or reverses, a cross-connection can pull contaminated water back into the clean supply, which is exactly what these devices are built to stop.</p>
    <p>State law requires annual testing by a certified tester, and Portland Water Bureau tracks every property with a device on file.</p>
    <p>Miss your test, miss your paperwork, and the consequences are real: fines, or in some cases a water shutoff, even if you actually paid for the test but the report never got filed.</p>
  </section>

